# Experiment storage is mandatory

Keep runnable code in existing code directories and new compact custody records
in `experiment_records/`. Generated media, arrays, caches, models, downloaded
review copies and intermediate payloads belong only in the configured external
`EXPERIMENT_RESULTS` store. Do not fall back into this checkout.

Read `.research/README.md`. New or changed writers must use
`scripts/research_storage.py` to validate destinations before writing. Immediately
record accepted CWC job IDs with `research_artifacts.remember_job()`; collect and
locate artifacts by job/artifact ID, relative store path, size and SHA-256.
Record source/intermediate dependencies as canonical storage references and hashes,
never Windows/Linux mount paths. Do not search arbitrary folders or rerun compute
because a local copy is missing; reconcile CWC IDs and retain any incident ID.

Run `python3 -B .research/storage_guard.py --staged --filesystem` before committing.
Install hooks with `python3 .research/install.py` on each checkout. Never disable
hooks, use `--no-verify`, regenerate historical exemptions or add payload ignore
exceptions. Preserve historical evidence. Missing/sync-pending/404 states are
not proof of permanent loss or scientific approval.
